{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178346-4th-nephandi-faction","id":1178346,"title":"4th Nephandi faction?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-22T21:49:08-08:00","id":1178346,"title":"4th Nephandi faction?","content":"So there are the Infernalists, who serve the demons and dark gods of human belief and legend that dwell in the High Umbra.<br /> <br /> There are the Malfean Nephandi, who serve the animistic spirits of entropy, consumption, and corruption that dwell in the Middle Umbra (i.e. the heads of the Wyrm and the Malejin Incarnae).<br /> <br /> And there are the K'llashaa who serve the completely alien Lords of the Outer Darkness in the Deep Umbra - basically Lovecraftian Outer Gods.<br /> <br /> <br /> These line up has a prominent piece missing. Those Low Umbra aligned Nephandi, who would specifically be Oblivion worshipers who take their commands from the restless dreams of the... well unfortunately the reused term is Malfeans... but ala Exalted after 1st edition, lets avoid reusing that term and just focus on the Neverborn. It doesn't seem like an ideology that would be any harder to gain loyalty to than any of the others. In fact I can easily see a fallen Euthanatos justifying how the entirety of existence must be given the Good Death*, or a fallen Akashic explaining how oblivation of the universe is the natural extension of obliviation of the self. The Labyrinth itself serves the natural role of Caul for these Mages to walk.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>*before anyone suggests it - no Voormas is not a jhor/oblivion aligned Nephandus in this regard. He's utterly evil, but his motivations actually run to the opposing extreme. He wants to bring the shroud down to remove distinction between the living and the dead to exist eternal - an anathemic inversion of Euthanatos ideology into that of a fantasy-fiction necromancer; not the ideology of the Euthanatos taken to cosmic extreme.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Of course I realize that the reason this wasn't one of the Nephandi factions, is Mage 1st edition had its own cosmology to go off of, and Werewolf's (VtM not having introduced broader cosmology). Wraith didn't exist yet to provide inspiration in this regard. But it still seems like something that should have shown up later, given structural repetition of threats through different aspects of the Umbra.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, how do Nephandi in East Asia divide themselves? The same way, or do they organize into allegiance to the Yama Kings? Or are those who serve Yang-aligned Yama Kings by definition &quot;Malfean&quot;, while those who serve Yin-aligned Yama Kings... well I suppose it would have to be this undiscussed in canon Oblivion-bound faction, wouldn't it? Dragons of the East didn't discuss Nephandi did it?<br /> <br /> <br /> I suppose we could discuss whether the Fomorian Dream might call its own Nephandi to serve, keeping up the parallelism along different aspects of the Umbra, but that might be overkill :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T23:21:14-08:00","id":1178377,"title":"","content":"Honestly I'd drop the First Group from Nephandi, I feel like them and the Yama King aligned Infernalists are more in common Awakening Seers than &quot;I've inverted my soul in the cauls and believe in the end of all things&quot; they just have aligned themselves with monsters for power.(They might even in theory escape!.. well the Yama King ones)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T01:15:23-08:00","id":1178383,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I wouldn't consider infernalists a nephandi faction, just a separate group with a good amount of overlap. Iirc you're even allowed to be an infernalist as long as you don't serve any demons from a JudaeoChristian source. At least, the order of Hermes sourcebook said something to that effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20546-dragonchild","name":"Dragonchild","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T01:16:36-08:00","id":1178384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonchild</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178346-4th-nephandi-faction?p=1178383#post1178383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I wouldn't consider infernalists a nephandi faction, just a separate group with a good amount of overlap. Iirc you're even allowed to be an infernalist as long as you don't serve any demons from a Christian source.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There are Infernalists who aren't Nephandi, but Infernal Nephandi have always been presented as one of the Nephandi factions in canon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T01:27:35-08:00","id":1178386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178346-4th-nephandi-faction?p=1178384#post1178384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> There are Infernalists who aren't Nephandi, but Infernal Nephandi have always been presented as one of the Nephandi factions in canon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand that, but it isn't kind of weird to categorize them based solely on the fact that they're also infernalists? Even barrabi are semi lumped together and they're all evil versions of the nine traditions which are really diverse. <br /> <br /> Also like lian said they often seem more interested in power than in the end of all things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20546-dragonchild","name":"Dragonchild","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T01:51:08-08:00","id":1178388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonchild</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178346-4th-nephandi-faction?p=1178386#post1178386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I understand that, but it isn't kind of weird to categorize them based solely on the fact that they're also infernalists? Even barrabi are semi lumped together and they're all evil versions of the nine traditions which are really diverse.<br /> <br /> Also like lian said they often seem more interested in power than in the end of all things.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not really - not when the other factions are also categorized by who their bosses are. They're not categorized as a faction because they happen to practice Infernalism. They're categorized as a faction because (unlike other Mage infernalists) they've actively ENSLAVED themselves to the same general category of spirit-bosses. It's the same reason Malfean Nephandi are a category - because they have enslaved themselves to the Maeljin Incarnae. <br /> <br /> Stephenls wrote some good posts on this like 12 years ago actually...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?250804-oMage-Nephandi&amp;p=5422106#post5422106\" target=\"_blank\">https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php...06#post5422106</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?250804-oMage-Nephandi&amp;p=5422261#post5422261\" target=\"_blank\">https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php...61#post5422261</a><br /> <br /> The second post is specifically on their factions. He argues though that the distinction is relatively arbitrary because Nephandi only enslave themselves like they do because it's part of the process of self-annihilation.<br /> <br /> Barabbi aren't really that &quot;lumped together&quot; - it's just a general category that refers to not being widderslainte. They aren't a faction, they're just what you call a Nephandus that joined up in their current lifetime, as opposed to Awakening already as Nephandi.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Interestingly noticed in that thread that there's been some suggestion that all of the Nephandi bosses are just dreams of the Neverborn, which is why no Nephandi serve the Neverborn directly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T01:54:05-08:00","id":1178389,"title":"","content":"Common Infernalist: made a really bad deal, but the power is just too damn alluring<br /> <br /> Nephandi infernalist: the world\u2019s going to hell, better save ourselves a good seat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T04:42:08-08:00","id":1178405,"title":"","content":"In the Revised Book of Madness it was stated that some of the Nephandi do serve the Neverborn, or at least that the things they serve were emanations of the dreaming Neverborn. I think it was even implied that some of the K'llashaa were those emanations. It was also stated in the revised Core that a lot of Nephandi lost their power when the 6th Great Maelstrom hit because it woke the Neverborn up (hence no dreams).<br /> <br /> As I recall, this power loss was specifically retconned by M20, but that was more because it was heavily pushing the idea that Nephandi don't get their power through servitude and, indeed, don't really serve.<br /> <br /> To me, it makes sense that the Neverborn (or their dreams) could be some of, but not all of, the K'llashaa. If the K'llashaa are monstrosities from outside the world as we know it, the Neverborn fit that description. That their origin story is known doesn't make it any less alien.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 01-23-2018, 07:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T09:09:02-08:00","id":1178451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178346-4th-nephandi-faction#post1178346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, how do Nephandi in East Asia divide themselves? The same way, or do they organize into allegiance to the Yama Kings? Or are those who serve Yang-aligned Yama Kings by definition &quot;Malfean&quot;, while those who serve Yin-aligned Yama Kings... well I suppose it would have to be this undiscussed in canon Oblivion-bound faction, wouldn't it? Dragons of the East didn't discuss Nephandi did it?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is fascinating for me how different persons can think and feel differently about such categorizations.<br /> For me it's obvious that Yama King and Queen - aligned Nephandi are the Asian equivalent of the Western Infernal Nephandi. Whether they are one sub-faction within the Nephandi faction is an interesting question. I'd say that they are a seperate sub-faction within the Nephandi from the Western Infernal Nephandi.<br /> The Malfean Nephandi should be present in Asia; though they see and call the Wyrm by the name 'Centipede'.<br /> I'd say that the Nephandi True Mages of the K'llashaa sub-faction have a strong tendency towards being similar to other K'llashaa Nephandi, regardless of the the location; and they are present all over the world.<br /> <br /> This is all said under the assumption that there are non-Western Nephandi True Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 01-24-2018, 03:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T12:07:40-08:00","id":1178504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178346-4th-nephandi-faction?p=1178451#post1178451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is all said under the assumption that there are non-Western Nephandi True Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>There most certainly would be. If nephandic influence can span the entire cosmos, there should be no reason they wouldn\u2019t be around outside of Europe on Earth.<br /> <br /> On that point, however, the k\u2019lashaa are a bit of an odd one. Cosmic Horrors as we know them where very much a western invention, starting from Lovecraft and continued by his contemporaries. Which means that no matter where these k\u2019lashaa come from, their culture is in many ways moulded by this western view of intangible horror.<br /> <br /> Intangible horror in the east doesn\u2019t really have an equivilant to the likes of yog-sothoth. Eastern horror tends to be much more \u201cpurposeful\u201d in a way. The bakemono act like strange animals, or tricksters with a plot. Demons are brutes. Dragons tend to be doing it for hunger, the gods are angry, or the ghosts are vengeful. I struggle to think of anything not directly modled off Lovecraft which reaches the same feel of complete incomprehensibility.<br /> <br /> The closest thing that comes to mind is something like Uzumaki from Junji Ito. Where the malevolent force is a pattern, a spiral.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 01-23-2018, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T12:17:51-08:00","id":1178508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178346-4th-nephandi-faction?p=1178504#post1178504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There most certainly would be. If nephandic influence can span the entire cosmos, there should be no reason they wouldn\u2019t be around outside of Europe on Earth..</div> </div> </div> </div>I would assume that\u2019s the case, but you never know in the WoD. East Asia is effectively its own cosmos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T12:34:37-08:00","id":1178510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">On that point, however, the k\u2019lashaa are a bit of an odd one. Cosmic Horrors as we know them where very much a western invention, starting from Lovecraft and continued by his contemporaries. Which means that no matter where these k\u2019lashaa come from, their culture is in many ways moulded by this western view of intangible horror.<br /> <br /> Intangible horror in the east doesn\u2019t really have an equivilant to the likes of yog-sothoth. Eastern horror tends to be much more \u201cpurposeful\u201d in a way. The bakemono act like strange animals, or tricksters with a plot. Demons are brutes. Dragons tend to be doing it for hunger, the gods are angry, or the ghosts are vengeful. I struggle to think of anything not directly modled off Lovecraft which reaches the same feel of complete incomprehensibility.<br /> <br /> The closest thing that comes to mind is something like Uzumaki from Junji Ito. Where the malevolent force is a pattern, a spiral.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly, but in WoD (and in the Mythos too, btw), cosmic horrors were &quot;created&quot; eons ago. Possibly before humanity. At least some seem to be the nightmares of the Neverborn (which may have been asleep from the beguinning of Creation), while others are a total mystery.<br /> <br /> Hence, yes, there's &quot;equivilant to the likes of yog-sothoth&quot; in China, it's just that the folklore and legens don't speak about them (Just like they don't speak about them in Europe nor in America)<br /> <br /> Or, to put it other way: Why do you think that Occident can have yog-sothoth cults that date from Cruzade (at the very least, because k\u2019lashaa are mentioned in the book about Infernalists), in spite of the fact this is a &quot;modern invention&quot;, as you say, and China can't?.<br /> <br /> I think most of WoD misrepresentation of other countries has to do with this weird idea that makes people to think that &quot;non-western&quot; places are supposed to be immersed in their own cultures, so to speak. It's borderline racist to think that most Chinese Nephandi have to be &quot;culturally appropiate&quot;, when you don't demand the same for &quot;the West&quot;.<br /> <br /> People in Asia read Lovecraft too, you know...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. They may want to use k\u2019lashaa concepts too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-23-2018, 03:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T14:10:41-08:00","id":1178547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178346-4th-nephandi-faction?p=1178504#post1178504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There most certainly would be. If nephandic influence can span the entire cosmos, there should be no reason they wouldn\u2019t be around outside of Europe on Earth.<br /> <br /> On that point, however, the k\u2019lashaa are a bit of an odd one. Cosmic Horrors as we know them where very much a western invention, starting from Lovecraft and continued by his contemporaries. Which means that no matter where these k\u2019lashaa come from, their culture is in many ways moulded by this western view of intangible horror.<br /> <br /> Intangible horror in the east doesn\u2019t really have an equivilant to the likes of yog-sothoth. Eastern horror tends to be much more \u201cpurposeful\u201d in a way. The bakemono act like strange animals, or tricksters with a plot. Demons are brutes. Dragons tend to be doing it for hunger, the gods are angry, or the ghosts are vengeful. I struggle to think of anything not directly modled off Lovecraft which reaches the same feel of complete incomprehensibility.<br /> <br /> The closest thing that comes to mind is something like Uzumaki from Junji Ito. Where the malevolent force is a pattern, a spiral.</div> </div> </div> </div>in the wod the mad arab prophet that lovecraft quoted is probably real.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> and so on. so it's more of a case of Lovecraft reminding humanity of cosmic horrors once again","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T14:51:36-08:00","id":1178560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178346-4th-nephandi-faction?p=1178510#post1178510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People in Asia read Lovecraft too, you know...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. They may want to use k\u2019lashaa concepts too.</div> </div> </div> </div>i.e. Uzumaki","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T18:28:17-08:00","id":1178639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178346-4th-nephandi-faction?p=1178451#post1178451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is fascinating for me how different persons can think and feel differently about such categorizations.<br /> For me it's obvious that Yama King and Queen - aligned Nephandi are the Asian equivalent of the Western Infernal Nephandi. Whether they are one sub-faction within the Nephandi faction is an interesting question. I'd say that they are a seperate sub-faction within the Nephandi from the Western Infernal Nephandi.<br /> The Malfean Nephandi should be present in Asia; though they see and call the Wyrm by the name 'Centipede'.<br /> I'd say that the Nephandi True Mages of the K'llashaa sub-faction have a strong tendency towards being similar to each same no matter the location; and they are present all over the world.<br /> <br /> This is all said under the assumption that there are non-Western Nephandi True Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can definitely see that logic. The counter-argument though is that the authority of the Maeljin Incarnae doesn't extend to East Asia, and instead the Yama Kings are the Centipede's direct agents in the struggles of the Beast Courts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T21:45:28-08:00","id":1178674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178346-4th-nephandi-faction?p=1178639#post1178639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I can definitely see that logic. The counter-argument though is that the authority of the Maeljin Incarnae doesn't extend to East Asia, and instead the Yama Kings are the Centipede's direct agents in the struggles of the Beast Courts.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Except the aren't? They can't grant gifts or any powers to Fallen Fera ala the Wyrm variants they have to reconstruct them with new whole sale powers.<br /> <br /> <br /> Having Read STephenl's work before I am not sure I agree the vast majority of &quot;Mages who serve Demons&quot;(WHich I would include Mage Akuma under) are Nephandi, that in fact the vast majority have avatars even if they are enslaved by Demons. I can see the logic if those who are on the Path of Descension doing so but I think there's plenty who just.. sort of fell off the path. Like Voormas.<br /> <br /> The part of this I consider important is the Yomi book is pretty explicit that in theory even your full on &quot;I've sworm the pact of Ebony and Jade&quot; and given my soul away Akuma.. can steal their souls back. Like their soul is sitting in an item in Hell.. that they could go all Ocean's 11 and escape with. Which doesn't quite line up with true believers in Descension.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T21:48:23-08:00","id":1178675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178346-4th-nephandi-faction?p=1178674#post1178674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Except the aren't? They can't grant gifts or any powers to Fallen Fera ala the Wyrm variants they have to reconstruct them with new whole sale powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>What? What does that have to do with whether or not the Yama Kings are presented as the Centipede's greatest agents in the &quot;of the East&quot; cosmology?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T21:54:13-08:00","id":1178677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178346-4th-nephandi-faction?p=1178675#post1178675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What? What does that have to do with whether or not the Yama Kings are presented as the Centipede's greatest agents in the &quot;of the East&quot; cosmology?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They are not presented as such explicitly? Kumo don't serve Yama Kings. a Kumo corrupts a Hakken to walk the spiral.. they have nothing to do with the Yama Kings. A KItsune for example who does the whole Yama King thing, loses all Gifts and Gnosis. Yama Kings are incapable of supporting Gnosis.<br /> <br /> This would seem to support the idea that they are not the direct agents of the Centipede but rather something related?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T22:05:00-08:00","id":1178682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178346-4th-nephandi-faction?p=1178510#post1178510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Possibly, but in WoD (and in the Mythos too, btw), cosmic horrors were &quot;created&quot; eons ago. Possibly before humanity. At least some seem to be the nightmares of the Neverborn (which may have been asleep from the beguinning of Creation), while others are a total mystery.<br /> <br /> Hence, yes, there's &quot;equivilant to the likes of yog-sothoth&quot; in China, it's just that the folklore and legens don't speak about them (Just like they don't speak about them in Europe nor in America)<br /> <br /> Or, to put it other way: Why do you think that Occident can have yog-sothoth cults that date from Cruzade (at the very least, because k\u2019lashaa are mentioned in the book about Infernalists), in spite of the fact this is a &quot;modern invention&quot;, as you say, and China can't?.<br /> <br /> I think most of WoD misrepresentation of other countries has to do with this weird idea that makes people to think that &quot;non-western&quot; places are supposed to be immersed in their own cultures, so to speak. It's borderline racist to think that most Chinese Nephandi have to be &quot;culturally appropiate&quot;, when you don't demand the same for &quot;the West&quot;.<br /> <br /> People in Asia read Lovecraft too, you know...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. They may want to use k\u2019lashaa concepts too.</div> </div> </div> </div>For further evidence, just look at Bloodborne. A Japanese interpretation of Lovecraft, and on the Western genre of Gothic literature (which I see as being a heavy influence on Lovecraft itself). Just like Dark Souls was a Japanese interpretation of Western high fantasy lit.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: Turning back to China, I'm reminded of an expression about Lovecraftian literature, and how it compares between America and Britain. It reads: in America the Old Secrets are very secret, while in Britain the Old Secrets are very old. Primarily, this difference stems from America having large space to hide &quot;Old Secrets&quot;, but having a relatively short history (that is, if you only count that history recorded by whites; Native American history is often ignored, what of it hasn't been lost). Britain, meanwhile, is a confined space, but with a long history, meaning Old Secrets go back very far.<br /> <br /> Now, imagine what sort of &quot;Old Secrets&quot; might arise in China, a land that is very large AND very old. What sort of horrors hide in the Middle Kingdom, that fall into deep cracks, and predate even the earliest of empires?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 01-24-2018, 01:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T00:13:48-08:00","id":1178692,"title":"","content":"There\u2019s at least one Korean wuxia webnovel that starts off as typical wuxia stuff... then it mixes up the genre with the Cthulhu Mythos. No, not \u2018Lovecraftian elements.\u2019 Straight-up Cthulhu Mythos, with Nyarlathotep referred to as \u2018the Devil Sleeping Beneath the Capital.\u2019 Along with elevating the eight half-mythical, half-historical god-emperors of China to the level of the Great Old Ones. Apparently the eight emperors struck a deal to postpone the devouring of the world by the Great Old Ones. And the deal\u2019s coming to its term.<br /> <br /> So no, I don\u2019t believe Cosmic Horror is solely European now. Perhaps it used to be, but no longer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T00:24:30-08:00","id":1178694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178346-4th-nephandi-faction?p=1178692#post1178692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There\u2019s at least one Korean wuxia webnovel that starts off as typical wuxia stuff... then it mixes up the genre with the Cthulhu Mythos. No, not \u2018Lovecraftian elements.\u2019 Straight-up Cthulhu Mythos, with Nyarlathotep referred to as \u2018the Devil Sleeping Beneath the Capital.\u2019 Along with elevating the eight half-mythical, half-historical god-emperors of China to the level of the Great Old Ones. Apparently the eight emperors struck a deal to postpone the devouring of the world by the Great Old Ones. And the deal\u2019s coming to its term.<br /> <br /> So no, I don\u2019t believe Cosmic Horror is solely European now. Perhaps it used to be, but no longer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, perhaps more accurately, no culture has a monopoly on ideas it generates. Memes are like fire; wherever it touches, it spreads. And the memes established by Lovecraft have spread far and wide, molding and shifting to accommodate successive cultures and time periods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T00:41:15-08:00","id":1178695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178346-4th-nephandi-faction?p=1178692#post1178692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There\u2019s at least one Korean wuxia webnovel that starts off as typical wuxia stuff... then it mixes up the genre with the Cthulhu Mythos. No, not \u2018Lovecraftian elements.\u2019 Straight-up Cthulhu Mythos, with Nyarlathotep referred to as \u2018the Devil Sleeping Beneath the Capital.\u2019 Along with elevating the eight half-mythical, half-historical god-emperors of China to the level of the Great Old Ones. Apparently the eight emperors struck a deal to postpone the devouring of the world by the Great Old Ones. And the deal\u2019s coming to its term.<br /> <br /> So no, I don\u2019t believe Cosmic Horror is solely European now. Perhaps it used to be, but no longer.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> While I agree with the premise i'm not sure I agree with how you got there. I mean Including Lovecraftian stuff doesn't intrinsically make it Cosmic Horror, Nyarko-chan is some mix of comedy and harem anime even if it does include all sorts of Lovecraftian entities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T00:48:37-08:00","id":1178697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178346-4th-nephandi-faction?p=1178695#post1178695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> While I agree with the premise i'm not sure I agree with how you got there. I mean Including Lovecraftian stuff doesn't intrinsically make it Cosmic Horror, Nyarko-chan is some mix of comedy and harem anime even if it does include all sorts of Lovecraftian entities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I wasn\u2019t clear. Stuff like Nyarko-chan is exactly what I meant by \u201cjust Lovecraftian elements,\u201d that is, a few pieces of the setting and flair of the Mythos. The example I posted has renowned old masters, ascended immortals, and all of Heaven itself scrambling around at the looming apocalypse, knowing full well that they\u2019re mere ants in front of the true rulers of the vast universe. Later in the novel, the Celestial Bureaucracy, the guys often jackass and dickish but who are ultimately protectors of humanity, is under siege by Cthulhu\u2019s cult. The writer is making it clear that no amount of typical wuxia asskickery isn\u2019t going to save the heroes. Isn\u2019t that Cosmic Horror?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T01:20:59-08:00","id":1178700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178346-4th-nephandi-faction?p=1178697#post1178697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry, I wasn\u2019t clear. Stuff like Nyarko-chan is exactly what I meant by \u201cjust Lovecraftian elements,\u201d that is, a few pieces of the setting and flair of the Mythos. The example I posted has renowned old masters, ascended immortals, and all of Heaven itself scrambling around at the looming apocalypse, knowing full well that they\u2019re mere ants in front of the true rulers of the vast universe. Later in the novel, the Celestial Bureaucracy, the guys often jackass and dickish but who are ultimately protectors of humanity, is under siege by Cthulhu\u2019s cult. The writer is making it clear that no amount of typical wuxia asskickery isn\u2019t going to save the heroes. Isn\u2019t that Cosmic Horror?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Depends how it ends really, I mean &quot;Punching Cthulhu in the Face&quot; is kind of its own subgenre.<br /> <br /> <br /> This doesn't mean there aren't full on examples of cosmic horror in Asian Media, and plenty of good cosmic horror that has nothing to do with Lovecraft either way.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T05:01:47-08:00","id":1178726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178346-4th-nephandi-faction?p=1178700#post1178700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Depends how it ends really, I mean &amp;quot;Punching Cthulhu in the Face&amp;quot; is kind of its own subgenre.<br /> <br /> <br /> This doesn't mean there aren't full on examples of cosmic horror in Asian Media, and plenty of good cosmic horror that has nothing to do with Lovecraft either way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed!<br /> <br /> Now, for the original topic... my limited lore kn Ascension tells me that the Nephandi are nihilists who pursue the world\u2019s death. If so, then maybe the reason there aren\u2019t Nephandi specifically following the Neverborn is, because they\u2019re already following them in a sense? The three factions, then, would be the method of Oblivion the Nephandi choose; immorality, corruption, and invasion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T05:45:46-08:00","id":1178741,"title":"","content":"Well, but why don't kill the intermediary?. If you serve the Neverborn, why not address them directly?<br /> <br /> Who knows?, The Book of the Fallen may adress them. <hr /><br /> Personally, I don't like ALL Nephandi being divided between whom they serve. Many Paradigms aren't about serving spirits and such. At the same time, some mages don't know Spirit/DimSci. It stands to reason that some fallen mages wouldn't have the inclination nor the means to contact &quot;patrons&quot; - particularly in the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> It makes sense for Nephandi to make deals with potent cosmic (or not so cosmic) horrors. They're the kind of people that have nothing to loose and at the same time have the arrogance to spit at the heaven - they won't be afraid to search for power in the most terrible places. However, I don't see why all Nephandy should do this (nor be consistent with their patrons of choice).<br /> <br /> I can see patronless Nephandy being a thing. They can believe in the abstract Disolution just as Choristers believe in the One without summoning any particular entity (not all Choristers have actual deals with heavenly entities) or maybe they believe on other kinds of apocalypse (a Technocrat wanting to erase humanity Fallout style? . Everything it's wrong, we need to delete the System and start anew)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T08:00:01-08:00","id":1178790,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s more or less addressed in the books. It\u2019s stated that malfeans may not all necessarily believe in the wyrm, but rather consider the wyrm a concept, an anthropomorphic personification of all the putrid waste that is mankind. They don\u2019t serve the wyrm so much as acknowledge that mankind is the wyrm, and that anyone trying to \u2018ascend\u2019 from that is acting out of sheer arrogance.<br /> <br /> Extrapolating from that, infernalist nephandi might not be religious. They might actually be nihilists or atheists. They see the world is already hell, so they might as well act the role of the demon. Everyone considers themselves the good guy of their own story, that level of pride must be punished.<br /> <br /> And the k\u2019lashaa may not even consider themselves beholden to a god, but rather a philosophy so twisted it resembles a creature outside of understanding. After all, the cosmic horrors of Lovecraft was born out of Lovecraft\u2019s own feelings of fragility and insignificance in the wake and resolve of the Great War, where powerful nations act as beings out of time, caring little for the people that crawl across its face.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 01-24-2018, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T08:51:13-08:00","id":1178812,"title":"","content":"There are elements of the Nephandi chapter in M20 I'm not thrilled about, but I love the idea that they don't serve dark forces so much as ally with them or use the appearance of servitude to their advantage. I also really enjoy the insinuation that they are actually as dangerous to their 'patrons' as they are to everything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T13:07:40-08:00","id":1178909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178346-4th-nephandi-faction?p=1178790#post1178790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Extrapolating from that, infernalist nephandi might not be religious. They might actually be nihilists or atheists. They see the world is already hell, so they might as well act the role of the demon. Everyone considers themselves the good guy of their own story, that level of pride must be punished.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Infernal Nephandi could perhaps also have among their numbers those True Mages who think and believe that by including the infernal in their True Magick (and other actions), by default and as the basic state of things they are invoking the concepts and the ideas rather than - as many for example Traditions True Mages consider it - invoking (for example) a specific infernal personage, hellish location or a kind of demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 01-24-2018, 04:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T16:09:17-08:00","id":1178988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178346-4th-nephandi-faction?p=1178405#post1178405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Revised Book of Madness it was stated that some of the Nephandi do serve the Neverborn, or at least that the things they serve were emanations of the dreaming Neverborn. I think it was even implied that some of the K'llashaa were those emanations. It was also stated in the revised Core that a lot of Nephandi lost their power when the 6th Great Maelstrom hit because it woke the Neverborn up (hence no dreams).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the gods/demons of the Nephandi are supposed to be the dreams of the sleeping (at least according to Rich Dansky). So the forces of Oblivion are ultimately behind everything, which makes a lot of sense - Nephandi want to murder the world after all. That is why there is no Oblivion faction - all the factions serve Oblivion. Any Nephwrack cults and the like would probably point towards one of the existing factions, most likely the Infernalists as default, but possibly others.<br /> <br /> Presumably the more advanced Nephandi begin to realize this, but also accept that their existing masters are just as good mediators between them and the Neverborns/Oblivion as going through some Spectres.<br /> <br /> This isn't just in Revised era. 1997's Book of Mirrors also talks about this.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T16:34:07-08:00","id":1178994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178346-4th-nephandi-faction?p=1178988#post1178988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, the gods/demons of the Nephandi are supposed to be the dreams of the sleeping (at least according to Rich Dansky). So the forces of Oblivion are ultimately behind everything, which makes a lot of sense - Nephandi want to murder the world after all. That is why there is no Oblivion faction - all the factions serve Oblivion. Any Nephwrack cults and the like would probably point towards one of the existing factions, most likely the Infernalists as default, but possibly others.<br /> <br /> Presumably the more advanced Nephandi begin to realize this, but also accept that their existing masters are just as good mediators between them and the Neverborns/Oblivion as going through some Spectres.<br /> <br /> This isn't just in Revised era. 1997's Book of Mirrors also talks about this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite, the wyrm is a very distinct and separate force from Oblivion, this is stated as much in Book of Worlds. While superficially they may want the same goals. Their rationale and methodology could not be more different.<br /> <br /> The wyrm seeks to undo the work of the weaver, and depending on how sympathetic you are towards the weaver, it's either to put the weaver out of her misery, revenge for taking over, or out of general malevolence. Most likely a mixture of all three. They wyrm seeks destruction and corruption of all that is made and ordered. It seeks to put an end to all things, to return all that was risen back to the slime it came from. All metal rusts, all buildings crumble, all flesh rots, in the service to bringing the world back to what it has always been.<br /> <br /> Oblivion just feeds. It does not avenge, plot, or scheme, it only feeds. Those that serve oblivion do so out of compulsion, out of giving in to the dark urge which sits within us all. There is no reason or rationale behind its desire for the end, no insanity neither to mask the end. While the Wyrm enforces corruption upon its enemies to drive them to its ranks, Oblivion quietly waits for souls to come to it. Oblivion has no need to rally the troops, the world's end is a certainty, it only needs to wait and consume what comes its way.<br /> <br /> The Wyrm is an almighty scream, a roar of fury which throws itself out from the pits of your stomach, a gaping bellow of terror and anger which empties your lungs of every ounce of air.<br /> While Oblivion is the silence that hangs in the air, just before you draw your next breath.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T16:44:02-08:00","id":1178998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178346-4th-nephandi-faction?p=1178994#post1178994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not quite, the wyrm is a very distinct and separate force from Oblivion, this is stated as much in Book of Worlds. While superficially they may want the same goals. Their rationale and methodology could not be more different.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sources conflict. The Books of Madness treat it as a secret truth of the Nephandi that all the other dark masters (including the Wyrm) are the mad dreams of the Neverborn. Obviously that isn't true if you're playing Werewolf! In Mage it's just a question of which source you're giving preeminence.<br /> <br /> My own table-canon is that Oblivion and the Wyrm are both equally real manifestations of the same truth playing out independently on different layers of the Umbra","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T16:47:58-08:00","id":1179004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178346-4th-nephandi-faction?p=1178998#post1178998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sources conflict. The Books of Madness treat it as a secret truth of the Nephandi that all the other dark masters (including the Wyrm) are the mad dreams of the Neverborn. Obviously that isn't true if you're playing Werewolf! In Mage it's just a question of which source you're giving preeminence.<br /> <br /> My own table-canon is that Oblivion and the Wyrm are both equally real manifestations of the same truth playing out independently on different layers of the Umbra</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like this and plan to use it in my own game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T17:02:12-08:00","id":1179012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178346-4th-nephandi-faction?p=1178998#post1178998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My own table-canon is that Oblivion and the Wyrm are both equally real manifestations of the same truth playing out independently on different layers of the Umbra</div> </div> </div> </div>In other Wraith books, they talk about how the forces of Oblivion are divided into two types - Kindlings and Barrows. Kindlings represent the active pursuit of destruction, while Barrows represent the passive side of Oblivion in silent desolation and ruin. Kindlings tend to be short term, but frenetic. Barrows take a long time to achieve fruition, but builds to be overwhelming.<br /> <br /> I've took that to mean the Barrows are the forces of Oblivion as it is typically known in Wraith, while Kindlings represent the active force of destruction - the Wyrm. The Wyrm serves Oblivion.<br /> <br /> The Triat is well known, but Wraith is much more metaphysical than Werewolf, and it is obvious Oblivion drives a whole lot, as does its mysterious and unnamed opposite that is responsible for Transcendence. Therefore, I've always believed there is a duality above the Triat, and Oblivion is one of its poles.<br /> <br /> As the Tao Te Ching says, &quot;The Tao begot one. One begot two. Two begot three. And three begot the ten thousand things.&quot;<br /> <br /> Werewolf has a lot of mythology about it. While I consider the Garou to have a lot more real knowledge and experience concerning the Middle Umbra, I've also believed that they don't know everything. And a lot of their philosophical explanations of the higher mysteries isn't actual knowledge, it is cultural myth. Their myth about the Weaver trapping the Wyrm is simply their religious explanation for the Problem of Evil in philosophy. It's dogma, not fact.<br /> <br /> For similar reasons, I also believe that the Maeljin Incarna (not the Elemental Maeljin) are simply the Garou's perception and names for negative Astral forces, what are called demons or devils in other game lines. Things like &quot;greed&quot;, &quot;hate&quot;, &quot;cruelty&quot;, etc. are not Middle Umbra concepts (which deals with the life cycles of the Earth), but are of the High Umbra.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T17:06:01-08:00","id":1179013,"title":"","content":"That's certainly consitent with the Kindred of the East interpretation of the cosmology, where Malfeas connects to the Yang-hells, and the Labyrinth connects to the Yin-hells.<br /> <br /> (which is ironic since the Hengeyokai associate the Centipede with Yin - seeing the healthy Triat not in the Western fashion of Chaos (Wyld) and Order (Weaver) supposed to be kept in balance by Destruction (Wyrm); but instead as Creation/Yang (Wyld) and Destruction/Yin (Wyrm) with the force of Preservation (Weaver) as Balance)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 01-24-2018, 08:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T18:35:07-08:00","id":1179039,"title":"","content":"So this all implies that Oblivion is the real big bad that's actually behind all the other dark and horrid things in WoD, be they wyrm, nephandi, spectre, or whatever.<br /> <br /> I guess it's only fitting the WoD is driven by Angst.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T21:39:01-08:00","id":1179103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178346-4th-nephandi-faction?p=1179039#post1179039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So this all implies that Oblivion is the real big bad that's actually behind all the other dark and horrid things in WoD, be they wyrm, nephandi, spectre, or whatever.<br /> <br /> I guess it's only fitting the WoD is driven by Angst.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now I'm imagining an alternate version of the apocalypse, where a team of characters from each gameline descend into Oblivion. And they encounter the final boss of the setting: an incredibly 90s king sitting on a black throne.<br /> <br /> And he introduces himself as the literal Edge Lord.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T07:11:42-08:00","id":1179182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178346-4th-nephandi-faction?p=1179103#post1179103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And he introduces himself as the literal Edge Lord.</div> </div> </div> </div>Extra points for his throne being half on the brim of oblivion. He doesn\u2019t sit on it much","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T07:49:20-08:00","id":1179194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178346-4th-nephandi-faction?p=1179039#post1179039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So this all implies that Oblivion is the real big bad that's actually behind all the other dark and horrid things in WoD, be they wyrm, nephandi, spectre, or whatever.<br /> <br /> I guess it's only fitting the WoD is driven by Angst.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on how much intent Oblivion has. My table canon for Wraith is that Oblivion doesn't want anything. It is an intensely corrosive force, sure, but it doesn't have an objective or even a mind. All of the hatred, sadism, and corruption of &quot;Oblivion&quot; comes from the Neverborn and the Spectres. Which doesn't stop Angst from being the driving force behind the corruption of the WoD, it just means that Angst doesn't come from Oblivion.<br /> <br /> If anything, Angst flows the other way...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T14:44:42-08:00","id":1179317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178346-4th-nephandi-faction?p=1179194#post1179194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Which doesn't stop Angst from being the driving force behind the corruption of the WoD, it just means that Angst doesn't come from Oblivion.<br /> <br /> If anything, Angst flows the other way...</div> </div> </div> </div>Oblivion is a pit of Angst...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T20:03:16-08:00","id":1179412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178346-4th-nephandi-faction?p=1179317#post1179317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oblivion is a bottomless pit of Angst...</div> </div> </div> </div>Fixed that for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20546-dragonchild","name":"Dragonchild","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T05:00:13-08:00","id":1179488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178346-4th-nephandi-faction?p=1179317#post1179317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oblivion is a pit of Angst...</div> </div> </div> </div>It consumes and annihilates Angst as easily as it does everything else. It consumes more of it than anything else, in fact, since Angst is partly the desire for self destruction. But if Angst is growing faster than it is being eaten, Oblivion isn't going to do anything to redress the balance. Oblivion doesn't care about balance.<br /> <br /> Oblivion doesn't care about anything.<br /> <br /> Oblivion doesn't care.<br /> <br /> Oblivion doesn't.<br /> <br /> Oblivion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T10:50:45-08:00","id":1179541,"title":"","content":"Does Oblivion have sentience? Or is it more like an abstract force like Time and Bad News?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T13:52:31-08:00","id":1179601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178346-4th-nephandi-faction?p=1179541#post1179541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Oblivion have sentience? Or is it more like an abstract force like Time and Bad News?</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely the latter. If you want an aware cosmic being looking to annihilate everything, look at the Wyrm. That's the one who makes the plans. That's the one who writhes in fury at the continued existence of all things, including itself. That is who WANTS to unmake the world.<br /> <br /> Oblivion is not a being, per se. It is the total <i>absence</i> of being. It does not have motives that exist, because it is the <i>antithesis</i> of existence. It does not want to unmake the world, because Want is a quality unique to beings. Oblivion is anti-being.<br /> <br /> Oblivion is not a monster that consumes, like the Wyrm. It's a yawning pit, that other things fall into when pushed. Nephandi, the Wyrm and its spawn, even the nihilistic, Oblivion-worshiping Specters, are the ones who do the pushing. But Oblivion, itself, merely accepts everything without care, thought, or pity.<br /> <br /> Oblivion is the ultimate passive force. It isn't a being. It just is. Or, rather, <i>IS NOT</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T13:53:02-08:00","id":1179602,"title":"","content":"Oblivion is not active and not sentient. It's just a force - basically entropy, but metaphysical. But its servants - those things tarred by their proximity to it - do have various kinds of sentience and activity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T13:59:28-08:00","id":1179603,"title":"","content":"&quot;A bottomless curse. A bottomless sea. Accepting of all that there is, and can be.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 01-26-2018, 05:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T14:31:30-08:00","id":1179617,"title":"","content":"Cool, so we\u2019ve established Oblivion and the Wyrm are very much not the same thing. Thank you for making my point so unanimously","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T16:29:49-08:00","id":1179653,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t think anyone at any point suggested they were the same thing. Just that there are different interrelationships suggested by different canons, and even different books in the same gameline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T16:32:09-08:00","id":1179656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178346-4th-nephandi-faction?p=1179602#post1179602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oblivion is not active and not sentient. It's just a force - basically entropy, but metaphysical. But its servants - those things tarred by their proximity to it - do have various kinds of sentience and activity.</div> </div> </div> </div>There also maybe intelligences in it. Especially if you adhere to the theory (which presumes One World of Darkness) that Oblivion is the Abyss of Obtenebration and the Hell of the Fallen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T22:43:26-08:00","id":1179753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178346-4th-nephandi-faction?p=1179653#post1179653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t think anyone at any point suggested they were the same thing. Just that there are different interrelationships suggested by different canons, and even different books in the same gameline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well there is a &quot;common&quot; view that the Wyrm is the one true baddy of the WOD rather than an Middle Umbral entirty representing much of that badness...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T14:25:53-08:00","id":1179937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178346-4th-nephandi-faction?p=1179541#post1179541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Oblivion have sentience? Or is it more like an abstract force like Time and Bad News?</div> </div> </div> </div>At my table it is the latter, definitely, and that's the idea I use whenever I'm looking at Wraith metaphysics. There are people who think the opposite though,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T16:10:50-08:00","id":1179966,"title":"","content":"I generally assume Oblivion has consciousness enough to \u201cHUNGER!\u201d but not self-awareness or intelligence enough to premeditate. That\u2019s what the Neverborn are for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T04:56:54-08:00","id":1180387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178346-4th-nephandi-faction?p=1179966#post1179966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I generally assume Oblivion has consciousness enough to \u201cHUNGER!\u201d but not self-awareness or intelligence enough to premeditate. That\u2019s what the Neverborn are for.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's precisely what they are for, and while they may be from Oblivion they aren't necessarily of Oblivion. It's not entirely clear why the Neverborn want to end the world although it is usually explained that they want to return to oblivion (desire to be annihilated) or they want to escape the world they are trapped in (desire to annihilate their bonds), but either way their desires are qualitatively different than Oblivion's.<br /> <br /> All of which can give fascinating inspiration for why a Nephandus would 'serve' a Neverborn or its sleeping emanations, or how they might go about manipulating one of the sleeping Malfeans.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T11:26:48-08:00","id":1180460,"title":"","content":"Almost two years ago I used to have some thoughts and ruminations about how some True Mages (including some of the Nephandi, maybe) could perhaps have one of the Stygian Deathlords, or Charon, as their patrons; with this changing a lot about how a Mage's True Magick would function. Though I have barely any idea about how this could and would work in practice and what exactly it would mean for the True Mage(s) and the Wraith(s) involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 01-29-2018, 02:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T16:07:58-08:00","id":1180526,"title":"","content":"Personally I favor ignoring Dansky's All Your Evils Are Belong to Wraith approach in favor of three kinds of Nephandi serving three kinds of masters with (at least) three very different philosophies and motivations that share the general motif of being evil/bad for John Q. Public and the specific methodology of warping their servants' souls into inverted parodies of their former selves via dipping in otherdimensional hazing rituals as a means of ensuring loyalty.<br /> <br /> As for the Neverborn, they don't have living mages serving them because they're so far down the rabbit hole they can't even perceive the world of the living or its inhabitants. They're a step removed from the spectres that wander an apocalyptic wasteland, able to spy the living but dimly and clearly perceive only wraiths; instead they can just barely catch glimmers of the Underworld and wraiths and only clearly discern spectres either in their presence in the labyrinth or through the hive mind when the latter venture higher up the metaphysical layers. Mages who venture down far enough to interact with them don't make it back alive. Some spectres like nephwracks might present themselves as creatures akin to demons when interacting with the living, but they lack the metaphysical oomph to twist reality and grant True Magick; all they can do is twist people's minds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T01:31:02-08:00","id":1180641,"title":"","content":"Sometimes I think the only reason they said that the K\u2019lashaa gods were the dreams of the neverborn was to just tie in the nephandi to Wraith after the fact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T05:16:42-08:00","id":1180670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178346-4th-nephandi-faction?p=1180526#post1180526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Neverborn, they don't have living mages serving them because they're so far down the rabbit hole they can't even perceive the world of the living or its inhabitants. They're a step removed from the spectres that wander an apocalyptic wasteland, able to spy the living but dimly and clearly perceive only wraiths; instead they can just barely catch glimmers of the Underworld and wraiths and only clearly discern spectres either in their presence in the labyrinth or through the hive mind when the latter venture higher up the metaphysical layers. Mages who venture down far enough to interact with them don't make it back alive. Some spectres like nephwracks might present themselves as creatures akin to demons when interacting with the living, but they lack the metaphysical oomph to twist reality and grant True Magick; all they can do is twist people's minds.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true of most Spectres, but I wouldn't extend that to the Neverborn. Instead their issue is that they find the world horrible and long for whatever they had before (whether that was Oblivion or some other world on the other side of it). Imagine for a moment that you fell through a gateway to another world where everything was made of bees and melting wax, the indigenous people communicated through infectious shrieking, and their emotions contaminated everything around them with the stench of fetid urine. Would you want to take a deeper look? Or would you rather huddle as close to the one source of blessed silence you could find and dream of that loathsome world vanishing?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178346-4th-nephandi-faction?p=1180641#post1180641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes I think the only reason they said that the K\u2019lashaa gods were the dreams of the neverborn was to just tie in the nephandi to Wraith after the fact.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly true. Certainly stating that all the Outer Lords were the dreams of the Neverborn was overdoing it. But if the Outer Lords are powerful alien monstrosities from strange realities who are dedicated to the destruction of the world as mages know it, well the Neverborn meet that definition. Theirs is just a different strange reality. In fact the only difference between them and the rest of the Outer Lords is one of location, and even then the Neverborn exist about as far from the world as it is possible to go in that direction.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T09:07:47-08:00","id":1180743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1178346-4th-nephandi-faction?p=1180641#post1180641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes I think the only reason they said that the K\u2019lashaa gods were the dreams of the neverborn was to just tie in the nephandi to Wraith after the fact.</div> </div> </div> </div>I strongly suspect it was because Dansky's vision of the World of Darkness is Wraith-centric (understandable, what with being the Wraith developer and all), and he disregarded what previous authors and developers had put together concerning the other game lines' antagonists when contributing to the Book of Madness. Because who cares about Werewolf and its made-up cosmology, or Mage and all the real-world folklore and mythology that inspired it, right? Wraith specialized in pulling an &quot;everything you thought you knew is WRONG!&quot; switcheroo on the makeup of the afterlife, which is fine for that line/setting but a slap in the face to the others and the work that had already been done on those settings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}